  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>An isothermal process is&nbsp;a thermodynamic process in which the temperature of a system remains constant. The transfer of heat into or out of the system happens so slowly that thermal equilibrium is maintained.</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>According to first law of thermodynamics,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
